For each claim, decide whether it is supported.

A claim is SUPPORTED when the cited text states it, or directly entails it: a
reader of the cited text alone would accept the claim as true without further
assumptions. Paraphrase, reordering, unit or number-format changes ("12,500"
vs "12500 people") and a correct simple restatement are fine.

A claim is NOT SUPPORTED when any part of it is missing from, goes beyond, or
contradicts the cited text. That includes:
- a different number, date, name or quantity than the cited text gives;
- an added detail, cause, comparison or qualifier the text doesn't state;
- a conclusion that needs outside knowledge or a multi-step inference;
- text that is merely on the same topic without stating the claim;
- a claim whose cited documents disagree with each other, unless the claim
  itself says that they disagree.

Judge every claim in the payload, in any order, once each. Give a short reason
that quotes or points to the deciding text (or says what is missing).

Respond with JSON of exactly this shape:

{"claims": [{"id": "<claim id>", "supported": true or false, "reason": "<one sentence>"}]}
